.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KLDLOAD-CONSOLE 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kldload-console
.Nd the operator console: a tmux session where each F-key opens a group of live views
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The terminal behind the web console's
.Pa /k9s/
page, and what
.Ql sudo kldload-console
opens over ssh: a
.Xr tmux 1
session named
.Ql kldload
that survives the page being reloaded.
The keys work without tmux's prefix:
F1 the home window; F2 k9s; F3 every kldload log; F4 the web console's
own logs; F5 to F12 groups of eBPF and cluster views \(em disk,
syscalls, TCP, Cilium, top, ZFS, tracing, what the kernel is short of \(em
each opened and closed by its key; the Shift+F keys single views; and
Alt with a letter quick pop-ups, Alt+b a chat with the assistant's model.
.Ql kldload-help cockpit
lists them all.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print the header comment and exit 0.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr tmux 1 ,
.Xr kinspect 8 ,
.Xr kldload-help 8 ,
.Xr kldload-session 8
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
Windows run as whoever started the console; in the web console that is
root.
